A||||4||My7Fieros||Get Jiggly with it............||||11||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||10-07-2000||09:54 PM||||Ok I know this has been covered before, but I need to know if its safe to drive around for a few days with a serious jiggly steering wheel. My roommate will fix it, but he's out of town until Weds (10-11)...some people on another thread (help! jiggly steering wheel...i revived it) talked about thiers..have any of you gotten it fixed? Did tightening the 4 bolts work? Im NOT buying another column for it (unless its absolutly necc.) so I need some input as to how hard it is and if it worked. I watched my roommate take off a couple of Fiero steering wheels to change the ignition...how much further down do you have to go? Thanx, Brian||||reg||11
Z||000001||theogre||10-07-2000||10:01 PM||||It won't fall off but no it's not safe.<P>It can be fixed. <P>how dificult it is depends on if you have the tools. You basically tear apart everything from the steering wheel to the dash. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||10-07-2000||10:05 PM||||Hmmm, well it seems to drive ok, its just kind of unsettling....<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 10-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||10-07-2000||11:49 PM||||Dont hold me to it, but you should be okay to drive around with it until Wed. I dont think it would ever fall off. I put an aftermarket steering wheel on, and I had a hell of a time getting the old one off. Finally have to use gear pullers, would have helped if somone would have told me they made a steering wheel puller tool in the first place. It is not difficult to remove the steering wheel if you have a puller, just unscrew the large center bolt holding it on, screw the steering wheel puller into the smaller holes around the center, and screw the steering wheel puller center bolt down until the steering wheel is loose. Make sure you make a mark on the wheel, and one on the colum to line it up properly for re-installation.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||10-08-2000||01:08 AM||||M7F, after you remove the wheel, remove the white turn signal asembly (it is held on with three Phillips head screws) as well as the lever detent (one phillips head screw). Remove the Hazard flasher unit from the outside of the steering column. Under the turn signal unit you will find three silver torx bolts - tighten these and it will tighten up the steering column. Also, make sure the four large bolts unter the dash are properly tightened.<P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                         <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT<p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 10-08-2000).]||||reg||1
